  "id": "spatial-coherence",
  "term": "spatial coherence",
  "definition": "Spatial coherence is the extent to which patterns in a signal stay similar or consistent across different locations. Weak spatial coherence means the pattern is more local and less globally shared, so consistency across space drops off quickly.",
